  "verbalization": "Certonardosterol D3 appears to have a direct relationship with JM1 through a series of intermediate targets. The evidence suggests that Certonardosterol D3 acts as a target for SNU-387, which in turn is a target of multiple compounds, including S-ethylcysteine zwitterion and Quercetagetin 3-methyl ether 7-glucoside. All of these compounds ultimately target JM1, indicating a potential pathway where Certonardosterol D3 influences JM1 via these intermediates. The consistent scores across the three paths suggest a robust, albeit indirect, connection between Certonardosterol D3 and JM1, likely through a series of molecular interactions that are not directly visible in the provided data. The mechanism appears to involve a cascade of targets, where Certonardosterol D3 serves as a starting point for a network of compounds that ultimately affect JM1. This integrated pathway highlights the importance of intermediates in drug action and underscores the complexity of molecular interactions in biological systems.",
